The answer to "close" carries the dialog's response: dbus_message_append_args()
takes the address of an INT32, not its value. With the response 0 (the
disclaimer accepted, a dialog's OK) libdbus got a NULL pointer and aborted
location-ui ("assertion value != NULL failed", signal 6), whenever a
liblocation client closed the dialog after its answer; any other response
was read as an address. Leste's build has the same line.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -586,7 +586,7 @@
 
 	new_msg = dbus_message_new_method_return(msg);
 	dbus_message_append_args(new_msg, DBUS_TYPE_INT32,
-				 dialog->dialog_response_code,
+				 &dialog->dialog_response_code,
 				 DBUS_TYPE_INVALID);
 
 	/* TODO: Review */
